    lines=['# Study013 — exact final-head coordinate robustness intervals','', '**Outcome:** exact, maximal signed16 code intervals were certified for all nine output biases and one descriptor-first weight per output row (column0). Every interval preserves all legally masked membership signs on627 canonical boards. The complete restored sets and raw-coordinate ties stay exact on4520 raw boards. This is a new parameter-space certificate, not a reranking of study008’s ±1 panel.','', '![All exact stored-code and delta intervals](intervals013.png)','', '## Frozen design and novelty','', 'Read studies008/009/010/011/012 before design. Study008 tested76 one-code attempts with no legal changes;009 changed many codes and row scales;010–012 tested symmetry and exact representations/ensembles. Here the question is the entire exact one-coordinate safe code interval, not a coarse conversion or score-space margin. Column0 is the lowest legal head input index chosen from actual descriptors, not from intervention damage. Study008 used column1; no coordinate replacement, outcome search, training or precision conversion occurs.','', f"Manifest SHA-256: `{result['manifest_sha256']}`. Model SHA-256: `{result['model_sha256']}`. Model is5195 bytes, unchanged. `manifest013.json` was chmod444 before ANY confirmation forwards or interval outcome computation. All copied inputs and source hashes were bound before confirmation.",'', '## Actual arithmetic and exact proof','', 'The final head has shape[9,8], source weights/biases signed16 in[-32768,32767], output signed32. Merged inputs use the frozen Q11 activation contract. Row exponents are[-12,-12,-12,-12,-12,-13,-12,-12,-12]; biases carry exponent-11 but runtime adds their decoded codes directly in activation/score integer units after row dot rounding. A bias code changeδ therefore addsδ to the preclamp output, notδ/2048 to the integer score. Effective real bias change isδ×2^-11. A weight changeδ changes the pre-round dot byδ×merged[j], with effective weight changeδ×2^row_exponent.','', 'Let D=2^(-row_exponent), R(a)=sign(a) floor((abs(a)+D/2)/D), and fixed bias b. Scores are clamp32(R(dot)+b). Clamping across the signed32 range preserves sign; no unclamped score is substituted for an output check. For an integer threshold t, the smallest dot giving R(dot)>=t is T(t)=tD-D/2 for t>0, and tD-(D-1)//2 for t<=0. For a weight code x, dot=other+merged[j]×x. A baseline member requires merged[j]×x>=T(-b)-other; a baseline nonmember requires the strict complement. For a bias code x, R(dot)+x>=0 iff x>=-R(dot). Intersect these integer half-lines over legal observations only, then intersect with signed16 source bounds. Occupied observations impose no policy constraints. Zero activation lanes impose a constant truth check, not a division.','', 'Monotonic scalar rounding and affine one-coordinate dependence make each per-board feasible set a half-line (or whole domain), so the intersection is contiguous. Thus the two endpoints and nearest failing in-range codes, together with the exact inequalities, certify maximality. An independent verifier additionally enumerates EVERY signed16 code, with no shared threshold formula, and recovers exactly the same intervals. None are joint/multi-parameter or universal-input certificates.','', '|Coordinate|Old code|Exact safe code interval|Exact safe delta interval|Lower/upper censored|','|---|---:|---|---|---|']
